    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"repeat\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f501\" role=\"img\" title=\"repeat\">:repeat:</span> pchickey submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14983#pullrequestreview-5657252986\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635121499,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793040245
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> pchickey created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14983#discussion_r4381122889\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Reading in a timeout loop is the wrong approach - we want a timeout for the total read, which should use <a href=\"https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/io/trait.AsyncReadExt.html#method.read_to_end\">AsyncReadExt::read_to_end</a>, not this loop that appends to the buffer (and uses a fragile heuristic for ending the response)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635121504,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793040246
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14983\">PR #14983</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635333514,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793094320
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> xia-chao submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14983#pullrequestreview-5665084293\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635334021,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793094443
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> xia-chao created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14983#discussion_r4387200403\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>you didn't consider that read to end waits for eof, and a keep alive 400 never closes the connection, so it just times out that's why the request sends connection: close.</p>\n</blockquote>",
